uage":38,"meta":44,"style":44},"dart pub global activate coverage\ndart test --coverage=coverage\ndart pub global run coverage:format_coverage --packages=.packages --report-on=lib --in=coverage --out=coverage\u002Flcov.info\n",[18,1781,1782,1797,1806],{"__ignoreMap":44},[48,1783,1784,1786,1788,1791,1794],{"class":50,"line":51},[48,1785,55],{"class":54},[48,1787,59],{"class":58},[48,1789,1790],{"class":58}," global",[48,1792,1793],{"class":58}," activate",[48,1795,1796],{"class":58}," coverage\n",[48,1798,1799,1801,1803],{"class":50,"line":87},[48,1800,55],{"class":54},[48,1802,286],{"class":58},[48,1804,1805],{"class":334}," --coverage=coverage\n",[48,1807,1808,1810,1812,1814,1817,1820,1823,1826,1829],{"class":50,"line":135},[48,1809,55],{"class":54},[48,1811,59],{"class":58},[48,1813,1790],{"class":58},[48,1815,1816],{"class":58}," run",[48,1818,1819],{"class":58}," coverage:format_coverage",[48,1821,1822],{"class":334}," --packages=.packages",[48,1824,1825],{"class":334}," --report-on=lib",[48,1827,1828],{"class":334}," --in=coverage",[48,1830,1831],{"class":334}," --out=coverage\u002Flcov.info\n",[14,1833,1834,1835,1838],{},"Or use ",[18,1836,1837],{},"genhtml"," (from lcov) to generate HTML reports.",[31,1840,1842],{"id":1841},"tips-tricks","💡 Tips & Tricks",[1743,1844,1845,1856,1868,1885,1909],{},[1746,1846,1847,1851,1852,1855],{},[1848,1849,1850],"strong",{},"Idiom",": name tests as sentences — ",[18,1853,1854],{},"test('Stack.pop returns the top item', ...)",". The output reads like a spec: \"Stack.pop returns the top item ... PASSED\". Describes behavior, not implementation.",[1746,1857,1858,1860,1861,1863,1864,1867],{},[1848,1859,1850],{},": use ",[18,1862,611],{}," to organize tests by class\u002Ffeature — ",[18,1865,1866],{},"group('Stack', () { test('push...', ...); test('pop...', ...); })",". The output shows the hierarchy, making test reports readable.",[1746,1869,1870,1860,1872,1874,1875,1877,1878,1881,1882,1884],{},[1848,1871,1850],{},[18,1873,724],{},"\u002F",[18,1876,728],{}," for fresh state per test — each test gets a clean ",[18,1879,1880],{},"Stack"," instance. Avoids test interdependence (one test's side effects don't affect another). ",[18,1883,724],{}," runs before each test.",[1746,1886,1887,1889,1890,1892,1893,1895,1896,1898,1899,1901,1902,1905,1906,1908],{},[1848,1888,1850],{},": prefer ",[18,1891,1397],{}," over ",[18,1894,1155],{}," — ",[18,1897,1397],{}," doesn't need code generation (",[18,1900,1382],{},"), just ",[18,1903,1904],{},"extends Mock implements X",". Simpler setup, same functionality. Use ",[18,1907,1587],{}," with a lambda.",[1746,1910,1911,1913,1914,1761,1916,1918,1919,1921],{},[1848,1912,1850],{},": write one test file per source file — ",[18,1915,1760],{},[18,1917,1764],{},". Keeps tests co-organized with code. Use ",[18,1920,611],{}," for sub-features within the file.",[31,1923,1925],{"id":1924},"️-edge-cases-gotchas","⚠️ Edge Cases & Gotchas",[1743,1927,1928,1946,1964,1986,2002,2023,2037,2056,2065,2075],{},[1746,1929,1930,93,1935,1937,1938,1941,1942,1945],{},[1848,1931,1932,1933],{},"Test files must end in ",[18,1934,1751],{},[18,1936,28],{}," only picks up files matching ",[18,1939,1940],{},"test\u002F**\u002F*_test.dart",". A file named ",[18,1943,1944],{},"test\u002Fstrings.dart"," is ignored.",[1746,1947,1948,93,1953,1956,1957,1960,1961,29],{},[1848,1949,1950,1952],{},[18,1951,324],{}," without a matcher is invalid",[18,1954,1955],{},"expect(value)"," doesn't compile. Use ",[18,1958,1959],{},"expect(value, equals(...))"," or ",[18,1962,1963],{},"expect(value, isTrue)",[1746,1965,1966,1974,1975,1978,1979,1981,1982,725,1984,29],{},[1848,1967,1968,1969,1874,1971,1973],{},"Async tests must be ",[18,1970,972],{},[18,1972,1147],{},"ed",": a test function that returns a ",[18,1976,1977],{},"Future"," but isn't marked ",[18,1980,972],{}," may finish before the future completes — the test passes\u002Ffails unpredictably. Make it ",[18,1983,972],{},[18,1985,1147],{},[1746,1987,1988,1997,1998,2001],{},[1848,1989,1990,1992,1993,286],{},[18,1991,724],{}," runs before ",[1994,1995,1996],"em",{},"each",": not once for the whole group. If setup is expensive, use ",[18,1999,2000],{},"setUpAll"," (runs once before all tests in the group) — but state isn't reset between tests.",[1746,2003,2004,93,2013,2015,2016,2018,2019,2022],{},[1848,2005,2006,2009,2010],{},[18,2007,2008],{},"throwsException"," vs ",[18,2011,2012],{},"throwsA(isA\u003CX>())",[18,2014,2008],{}," checks for an ",[18,2017,1106],{},"; ",[18,2020,2021],{},"throwsA(isA\u003CArgumentError>())"," checks for a specific type. Use the specific form for custom exceptions.",[1746,2024,2025,93,2028,2030,2031,2033,2034,2036],{},[1848,2026,2027],{},"Mockito needs code generation",[18,2029,1210],{}," + ",[18,2032,1382],{}," generates the mock file. Forgetting the build step gives \"missing mock file\" errors. ",[18,2035,1397],{}," avoids this.",[1746,2038,2039,2044,2045,2048,2049,2052,2053,2055],{},[1848,2040,2041],{},[18,2042,2043],{},"verify(...).called(1)",": checks the method was called exactly once. ",[18,2046,2047],{},"called(0)"," (never), ",[18,2050,2051],{},"called(greaterThan(1))"," (at least twice). Forgetting ",[18,2054,1360],{}," means you're not verifying the call.",[1746,2057,2058,2061,2062,2064],{},[1848,2059,2060],{},"Test isolation",": tests should be independent — one test's failure shouldn't cascade. Use ",[18,2063,724],{}," for fresh state; avoid shared mutable state across tests.",[1746,2066,2067,2070,2071,2074],{},[1848,2068,2069],{},"Coverage tooling",": Dart's coverage requires ",[18,2072,2073],{},"dart pub global activate coverage"," and a multi-step process. It's not as integrated as some languages' coverage. Use LCOV for reports.",[1746,2076,2077,2080],{},[1848,2078,2079],{},"Integration tests are slower",": unit tests (one class) are fast; integration tests (multiple components) are slower. Keep them separate and run unit tests frequently, integration tests in CI.",[31,2082,2084],{"id":2083},"spot-the-bug","🧠 Spot the Bug",[14,2086,2087],{},"A developer writes an async test, but it passes even when the code is broken:",[36,2089,2090],{"language":55},[40,2091,2093],{"className":111,"code":2092,"language":55,"meta":44,"style":44},"test('fetch returns data', () {\n    var future = fetchData();\n    expect(future, completion(equals('hello')));\n});\n",[18,2094,2095,2106,2119,2137],{"__ignoreMap":44},[48,2096,2097,2099,2101,2104],{"class":50,"line":51},[48,2098,20],{"class":54},[48,2100,152],{"class":83},[48,2102,2103],{"class":58},"'fetch returns data'",[48,2105,158],{"class":83},[48,2107,2108,2110,2113,2115,2117],{"class":50,"line":87},[48,2109,980],{"class":119},[48,2111,2112],{"class":83}," future ",[48,2114,778],{"class":119},[48,2116,991],{"class":54},[48,2118,994],{"class":83},[48,2120,2121,2123,2125,2127,2129,2131,2133,2135],{"class":50,"line":135},[48,2122,999],{"class":54},[48,2124,1045],{"class":83},[48,2126,1048],{"class":54},[48,2128,152],{"class":83},[48,2130,180],{"class":54},[48,2132,152],{"class":83},[48,2134,169],{"class":58},[48,2136,1059],{"class":83},[48,2138,2139],{"class":50,"line":147},[48,2140,1015],{"class":83},[14,2142,2143],{},"What's wrong?",[2145,2146,2147,2151,2164,2175,2290,2304],"details",{},[2148,2149,2150],"summary",{},"Answer",[14,2152,2153,2154,2156,2157,2159,2160,2163],{},"The test function isn't ",[18,2155,972],{}," and doesn't ",[18,2158,1147],{}," the expectation. ",[18,2161,2162],{},"expect(future, completion(...))"," registers an async expectation, but the test function returns immediately (synchronously) — the test framework thinks the test is done before the future completes. The async assertion may not run, so the test passes vacuously (false positive).",[14,2165,2166,2167,725,2169,2171,2172,2174],{},"The fix — make the test ",[18,2168,972],{},[18,2170,1147],{}," the expectation, or ",[18,2173,1147],{}," the future directly:",[40,2176,2178],{"className":111,"code":2177,"language":55,"meta":44,"style":44},"\u002F\u002F Option 1: await the expectation\ntest('fetch returns data', () async {\n    var future = fetchData();\n    await expectLater(future, completion(equals('hello')));\n});\n\n\u002F\u002F Option 2: await the future directly (cleaner)\ntest('fetch returns data', () async {\n    var data = await fetchData();\n    expect(data, equals('hello'));\n});\n",[18,2179,2180,2185,2199,2211,2231,2235,2239,2244,2258,2272,2286],{"__ignoreMap":44},[48,2181,2182],{"class":50,"line":51},[48,2183,2184],{"class":289},"\u002F\u002F Option 1: await the expectation\n",[48,2186,2187,2189,2191,2193,2195,2197],{"class":50,"line":87},[48,2188,20],{"class":54},[48,2190,152],{"class":83},[48,2192,2103],{"class":58},[48,2194,969],{"class":83},[48,2196,972],{"class":119},[48,2198,975],{"class":83},[48,2200,2201,2203,2205,2207,2209],{"class":50,"line":135},[48,2202,980],{"class":119},[48,2204,2112],{"class":83},[48,2206,778],{"class":119},[48,2208,991],{"class":54},[48,2210,994],{"class":83},[48,2212,2213,2215,2217,2219,2221,2223,2225,2227,2229],{"class":50,"line":147},[48,2214,1039],{"class":119},[48,2216,1042],{"class":54},[48,2218,1045],{"class":83},[48,2220,1048],{"class":54},[48,2222,152],{"class":83},[48,2224,180],{"class":54},[48,2226,152],{"class":83},[48,2228,169],{"class":58},[48,2230,1059],{"class":83},[48,2232,2233],{"class":50,"line":161},[48,2234,1015],{"class":83},[48,2236,2237],{"class":50,"line":191},[48,2238,132],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":131},[48,2240,2241],{"class":50,"line":197},[48,2242,2243],{"class":289},"\u002F\u002F Option 2: await the future directly (cleaner)\n",[48,2245,2246,2248,2250,2252,2254,2256],{"class":50,"line":202},[48,2247,20],{"class":54},[48,2249,152],{"class":83},[48,2251,2103],{"class":58},[48,2253,969],{"class":83},[48,2255,972],{"class":119},[48,2257,975],{"class":83},[48,2259,2260,2262,2264,2266,2268,2270],{"class":50,"line":214},[48,2261,980],{"class":119},[48,2263,983],{"class":83},[48,2265,778],{"class":119},[48,2267,988],{"class":119},[48,2269,991],{"class":54},[48,2271,994],{"class":83},[48,2273,2274,2276,2278,2280,2282,2284],{"class":50,"line":259},[48,2275,999],{"class":54},[48,2277,1002],{"class":83},[48,2279,180],{"class":54},[48,2281,152],{"class":83},[48,2283,169],{"class":58},[48,2285,188],{"class":83},[48,2287,2288],{"class":50,"line":264},[48,2289,1015],{"class":83},[14,2291,2292,2293,1874,2295,2297,2298,2300,2301,2303],{},"::\nWith ",[18,2294,972],{},[18,2296,1147],{},", the test function returns a ",[18,2299,1977],{},", and the framework waits for it to complete before evaluating pass\u002Ffail. Option 2 (await the future, then ",[18,2302,324],{},") is cleaner and more common.",[14,2305,2306,2309,2310,725,2312,2314,2315,1874,2317,2319,2320,725,2322,2324,2325,29],{},[1848,2307,2308],{},"The lesson",": async tests must be ",[18,2311,972],{},[18,2313,1147],{}," the async operation (or the expectation). Without ",[18,2316,972],{},[18,2318,1147],{},", the test function returns before the future completes, and the framework may finish the test prematurely (false positive). Make the test ",[18,2321,972],{},[18,2323,1147],{}," the result, then ",[18,2326,324],{},[31,2328,2329],{"id":2148},"Summary",[14,2331,2332,2333,245,2335,2337,2338,245,2340,1874,2342,2344,2345,1874,2347,245,2349,245,2352,1874,2354,2356,2357,2359,2360,2362,2363,2365,2366,2368],{},"You can write tests (",[18,2334,20],{},[18,2336,324],{},", matchers, ",[18,2339,611],{},[18,2341,724],{},[18,2343,728],{},"), test async code (",[18,2346,972],{},[18,2348,1147],{},[18,2350,2351],{},"expectLater",[18,2353,1048],{},[18,2355,546],{},"), mock dependencies (",[18,2358,1397],{}," simpler, ",[18,2361,1155],{}," with codegen), parameterize tests (loops), run with ",[18,2364,28],{},", and measure coverage — with the async-test-needs-await and ",[18,2367,1751],{},"-naming traps avoided. Next: Dart for the web.",[2370,2371,2372],"style",{},"html pre.shiki code .sIsaT, html code.shiki .sIsaT{--shiki-default:#6F42C1;--shiki-github-dark